  Version:       1.6.5
  Commit:        5102eddff28d9b605f3e6783d50ad380f61f692e
  Archive:       https://github.com/michaelrsweet/pdfio/releases/download/v1.6.5/pdfio-1.6.5.tar.gz
  SHA-256:       2b9e1db7c4a72cbc896098a6682a1e51fc2bfb979f00bec8bb515ee79c338084
  Imported:      2026-10-08
  License:       Apache-2.0 with exceptions (src/vendor/pdfio/LICENSE and
                 src/vendor/pdfio/NOTICE); ttf.c and ttf.h carry the same
  Local patches: applied in this order, from tools/patches/
                 0001-visibility-override.patch
                 0002-no-stdio.patch

src/vendor/pdfio/ is the files listed in tools/pdfio-files.txt, copied from
the release tarball, with exactly the patches above applied.
tools/verify-vendor re-derives the tree from the pinned tarball and the
patch series and fails on any other difference. Each patch adds a
modification notice to every file it changes (Apache-2.0 section 4(b)).

  0001-visibility-override  _PDFIO_PUBLIC and _PDFIO_PRIVATE can be defined
                            on the command line. pdfio marks its API
                            visibility("default"), which would export it
                            from zupdf.so past $(C_VISIBILITY); Makevars
                            defines both empty, so only R_init_zupdf is
                            exported.
  0002-no-stdio             PDFIO_NO_STDIO leaves out the default error
                            callback's fprintf(stderr), ttf's errorf()
                            fallback to stderr and the three DEBUG value
                            printers, which R CMD check reports as
                            console output. zupdf always installs its own
                            callbacks, so none of these is reachable.

Both are proposed upstream as build options; neither changes behaviour.

Only the library is imported: the sixteen pdfio-*.c translation units and
ttf.c, the headers they include, LICENSE and NOTICE. The examples (pdf2text.c
is ported as project code, design D10), tests, test files, documentation,
configure, Makefile.in and IDE projects are deliberately excluded.
HAVE_LIBPNG, HAVE_LIBWEBP and HAVE_GETRANDOM are never defined.

